From b4602cd531de4047d1c7f7ceb88acf45b20519a1
Subject: multiline: enter inserts newline, shift+enter submits
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy_simple_text_input/commit/b4602cd531de4047d1c7f7ceb88acf45b20519a1
Date: 2026-04-27T15:35:29+01:00

invert the default Enter/Shift+Enter bindings: in multiline mode plain
Enter inserts a newline and Shift+Enter (or NumpadEnter, or Alt+Enter on
macos) submits. single-line mode is unchanged: NewLine falls through to
the submit arm via Submit | NewLine.

also clear `select` in the submit arm so a held Shift modifier doesn't
preserve the old multi-line cursor anchor as a selection -- on the next
frame cosmic-text would try to shape an anchor on a line that no longer
exists and panic.
